# The Dutch are the world's tallest men. How tall were they a century earlier?
subtitle: "Guess how tall Dutch men born in 1896 were, then where they ranked back then, and what made a whole nation grow 13 centimetres."
tags: ["health","history","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Were they always giants?\" note \"1896 vs 1996\""

## The Dutch are the world's tallest men. How tall were they a century earlier?
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Average height of men by year of birth
      authors: Our World in Data, from NCD-RisC (2016)
      year: 2017
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/average-height-of-men
      finding: 'Dutch men born in 1996: 182.5 cm (tallest of 200 countries); born in 1896: 169.4 cm (12th, behind Sweden 171.9, Norway 171.2 and the US 171.1); US men 177.1 cm in both 1950 and 1996 cohorts; Iran grew most, +16.5 cm'
    - id: owid_height
      title: Human Height
      authors: Max Roser, Cameron Appel and Hannah Ritchie (Our World in Data)
      year: 2019
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/human-height
      finding: over generations, better nutrition and less disease in childhood made people taller; the Netherlands is the tallest population
    - id: ncd
      title: A century of trends in adult human height
      authors: NCD Risk Factor Collaboration (eLife)
      year: 2016
      finding: mean height of adults born 1896–1996 in 200 countries

